(** * SpendAuthG fixed-base window-sign (positive QR) computational certificate

    For every window [w] (0..84) and digit [i] (0..7) of the SpendAuthG
    fixed-base table, the true Weierstrass multiple's y-coordinate is the
    quadratic-residue-admitting root selected by the z-table:

      is_square
        (UnOp.from
          (EccSpec.fw_z <window w> +F
            Point.y (PallasModel.repr <multiple w i>))) = true

    where [<window w> = List.nth w
    OrchardActionFixedBase.spend_auth_g_fixed_table
    OrchardActionFixedBase.fixed_window_default] and the multiple
    [<multiple w i> = List.nth i (List.nth w SpendAuthGFullTable.full_table
    []) Pallas.identity] is read from the shared table leaf
    ([circuit_proof/spend_auth_g/table.v]) — the octupling-chain-computed
    table of all 85*8 = 680 multiples
    [Pallas.mul (window_scalar 85 w d) spend_auth_g_G].  The y-analogue of the
    x-coordinate certificate [SpendAuthGFixedWindowCert.x_check_true]; the
    per-entry extraction [y_check_entry] is consumed by the ladder file, whose
    [nonlast_points_correct]/[last_entry_eq_gen] bridge lemmas rewrite the
    [full_table] entry to [Pallas.mul (window_scalar 85 w d) spend_auth_g_G].

    The checker scaffolding is the shared [FixedBaseSignCert] section
    ([circuit_proof/cert_defs.v]); this file keeps only its
    [root_table] witness data and the single [vm_compute] certificate
    [root_check_true] — one field multiplication per entry over the table
    leaf's [full_table_reduced] literal, stated as the raw [forallb] term so
    the extraction type-checks syntactically.  If any entry's y were not the
    QR-admitting root (a genuine underconstraint: two admissible window-point
    signs), no root witness could exist and the certificate would fail rather
    than lie.  The QR chain is held [Strategy opaque] so the kernel's
    conversion oracle never expands [is_square] to a [modpow] over the
    concrete Pallas [(p-1)/2] exponent.  This file reads the shared table
    READ-ONLY — the octupling chain is paid once, there, by
    [full_table_reduced_eq], never here. *)

